{
  "id": "Compound::DB00493 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Cefotaxime is likely to interact with Slc22a6 through a shared mechanism involving organic anion transport. The evidence suggests that Cefotaxime binds to Slc22a11 or Slc22a8, which are both involved in organic anion transport. This transport process is mediated by Slc22a6, as these proteins are part of the same functional pathway. The binding of Cefotaxime to these transporters may influence their activity, potentially altering the transport of organic anions, including those of Cefotaxime itself. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a strong, albeit indirect, relationship, supported by the shared role of Slc22a6 in the transport process. The mechanism is further supported by the involvement of multiple Slc22 family members in anion transport, suggesting a broader functional context.",
